In the above code snippet:
- We are reading all comments (in the code) starting with "@@@" in the second part of code and printing all Assert statements related to them.
- We are assuming this code is executed in a debugging environment, and Debug is an already initialized class in such environments.
- In code, we have replaced the comment "// @@@ index of x in the new array is geq minus 1" with the appropriate Assert statement using PexObserve.ValueForViewing variables. The 'x' could hold any numerical value, so we're not asserting any equality between 'x' and its count in the list. Instead, this assertion checks if the IndexOf(x) is equivalent to or greater than -1.--------------------
